<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

  <!--
    WS-1 — the identity a Windows station runs a staff shift as.

    A station cannot use a cashier's own Odoo account, because front-of-house
    staff deliberately do not have one: they have a PIN against mezze.cashier.
    So the session runs as a shared SERVICE identity, and the accountability
    stays on the cashier recorded against the session and in the audit log.

    Two limits apply to that identity, and both are enforced by the server:

      * this group grants nothing beyond internal-user basics — no POS manager,
        no accounting, no settings;
      * a session opened for a station is CONFINED BY PATH before dispatch
        (domain/station_surface.py), so typing /odoo into a till reaches nothing.

    The second is the load-bearing one. Groups decide what a user may read; the
    path confinement decides that a station is a till and not a back office.
  -->
  <record id="group_station_service" model="res.groups">
    <field name="name">Mezze Station Service</field>
    <field name="comment">Least-privilege identity used by a Windows station for a staff
      shift. Never assign this to a person: it exists so a device-authenticated station
      can render the POS surfaces without any human's credential being stored on the
      till. Sessions using it are confined to the Mezze surfaces server-side.</field>
    <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(4, ref('base.group_user'))]"/>
  </record>

</odoo>
